  "worked_solution": "The coefficient of $(x+1)^{4}$ is given by $\\frac{{f}^{(4)}(-1)}{4!}.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{f}^{(4)}(-1)}{4!} & =\\frac{11}{24} \\\\ \\frac{{f}^{(4)}(-1)}{24} & =\\frac{11}{24} \\\\ {f}^{(4)}(-1) & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
